{"id":"mahabharata-10-012","work":"mahabharata","part":10,"partName":"सौप्तिकपर्व","partNameEn":"Sauptika Parva","unit":12,"title":"द्वादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 12 · Krishna warns of the Brahmashira","summary":{"en":"Krishna tells Yudhishthira that Drona's son knows the Brahmashira weapon and will use it when pressed, and that Bhima, enraged, must be followed. He urges haste, and Krishna, Arjuna and Yudhishthira ride out after Bhima.","kn":"ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮಶಿರಾಸ್ತ್ರ ತಿಳಿದಿದ್ದು ಒತ್ತಡದಲ್ಲಿ ಬಳಸುವನೆಂದೂ ಕೋಪಗೊಂಡ ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಅನುಸರಿಸಬೇಕೆಂದೂ ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತ್ವರೆ ಮಾಡಲು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೃಷ್ಣ, ಅರ್ಜುನ, ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರರು ಭೀಮನ ಹಿಂದೆ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"कृष्ण युधिष्ठिर से कहते हैं कि अश्वत्थामा ब्रह्मशिर अस्त्र जानता है और दबाव में उसे चलाएगा, इसलिए क्रुद्ध भीम का पीछा करना होगा। वे शीघ्रता करने को कहते हैं और कृष्ण, अर्जुन और युधिष्ठिर भीम के पीछे निकलते हैं।","te":"అశ్వత్థామకు బ్రహ్మశిరోస్త్రం తెలుసని, ఒత్తిడిలో దాన్ని ప్రయోగిస్తాడని, కోపించిన భీముని అనుసరించాలని కృష్ణుడు యుధిష్ఠిరునికి చెబుతాడు. తొందర చేయమంటాడు; కృష్ణుడు, అర్జునుడు, యుధిష్ఠిరుడు భీముని వెంట బయలుదేరతారు.","ta":"அஸ்வத்தாமன் பிரம்மசிர அஸ்திரத்தை அறிந்தவன், நெருக்கடியில் அதை எய்வான், எனவே சினமுற்ற பீமனைத் தொடர வேண்டும் என்று கண்ணன் யுதிஷ்டிரரிடம் கூறுகிறார். விரைய, கண்ணன், அர்ஜுனன், யுதிஷ்டிரர் பீமனைப் பின்தொடர்கின்றனர்.","ml":"ദ്രോണപുത്രന് ബ്രഹ്മശിരസ്സ് എന്ന അസ്ത്രം അറിയാമെന്നും, സമ്മർദ്ദത്തിലാകുമ്പോൾ അത് പ്രയോഗിക്കുമെന്നും കൃഷ്ണൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനോട് പറയുന്നു; കോപിച്ച ഭീമനെ പിന്തുടരണമെന്നും പറയുന്നു. വേഗത്തിൽ പോകണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം നിർദ്ദേശിക്കുന്നു; കൃഷ്ണനും അർജുനനും യുധിഷ്ഠിരനും ഭീമന്റെ പിന്നാലെ കുതിരപ്പുറത്ത് പുറപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 10.12; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Fri Oct 30 2026","sections":[{"title":"ऐषीकपर्व","titleEn":"Aishika Parva (The reed weapon)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्मिन्प्रयाते दुर्धर्षे यदूनामृषभस्ततः ।\nअब्रवीत्पुण्डरीकाक्षः कुन्तीपुत्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the invincible Bhima had gone, the lotus-eyed one, bull of the Yadus, said to Yudhishthira, son of Kunti."}},{"n":2,"text":"एष पाण्डव ते भ्राता पुत्रशोकमपारयन् ।\nजिघांसुर्द्रौणिमाक्रन्दे याति भारत भारतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pandava, this brother of yours, unable to bear grief for his sons, goes in the heat of the fight, wishing to kill Drona's son, O Bharata."}},{"n":3,"text":"भीमः प्रियस्ते सर्वेभ्यो भ्रातृभ्यो भरतर्षभ ।\nतं कृच्छ्रगतमद्य त्वं कस्मान्नाभ्यवपद्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima is the dearest of all your brothers, best of Bharatas; why do you not go to him today when he is in trouble?"}},{"n":4,"text":"यत्तदाचष्ट पुत्राय द्रोणः परपुरंजयः ।\nअस्त्रं ब्रह्मशिरो नाम दहेद्यत्पृथिवीमपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The weapon called Brahmashira, which Drona, conqueror of enemy cities, taught to his son, can burn even the earth."}},{"n":5,"text":"तन्महात्मा महाभागः केतुः सर्वधनुष्मताम् ।\nप्रत्यपादयदाचार्यः प्रीयमाणो धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled, fortunate teacher, the banner of all bowmen, gave that same weapon to Dhananjaya, being pleased with him."}},{"n":6,"text":"तत्पुत्रोऽस्यैवमेवैनमन्वयाचदमर्षणः ।\nततः प्रोवाच पुत्राय नातिहृष्टमना इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"His son, intolerant, begged it of him in the same way; then the father gave it to his son, not entirely happily."}},{"n":7,"text":"विदितं चापलं ह्यासीदात्मजस्य महात्मनः ।\nसर्वधर्मविदाचार्यो नान्विषत्सततं सुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He knew the fickleness of that great-souled son, and the teacher, who knew all dharma, was always wary of his son."}},{"n":8,"text":"परमापद्गतेनापि न स्म तात त्वया रणे ।\nइदमस्त्रं प्रयोक्तव्यं मानुषेषु विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said: \"Dear son, even in the greatest calamity you must never use this weapon in battle, least of all against men.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"इत्युक्तवान्गुरुः पुत्रं द्रोणः पश्चादथोक्तवान् ।\nन त्वं जातु सतां मार्गे स्थातेति पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"After telling his son so, Drona afterward added: \"Best of men, you will never stand on the path of the good.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"स तदाज्ञाय दुष्टात्मा पितुर्वचनमप्रियम् ।\nनिराशः सर्वकल्याणैः शोचन्पर्यपतन्महीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understanding his father's unwelcome words, the evil-minded one, hopeless of all good, grieved and fell to the ground."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततस्तदा कुरुश्रेष्ठ वनस्थे त्वयि भारत ।\nअवसद्द्वारकामेत्य वृष्णिभिः परमार्चितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O best of the Kurus, when you were living in the forest, O Bharata, he went to Dvaraka and lived there, greatly honored by the Vrishnis."}},{"n":12,"text":"स कदाचित्समुद्रान्ते वसन्द्रारवतीमनु ।\nएक एकं समागम्य मामुवाच हसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, when he was living by the sea near Dvaravati, he came to me alone and, as if smiling, said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"यत्तदुग्रं तपः कृष्ण चरन्सत्यपराक्रमः ।\nअगस्त्याद्भारताचार्यः प्रत्यपद्यत मे पिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Krishna, my father, the teacher of the Bharatas, true in valor, practicing fierce austerity, received from Agastya that weapon named Brahmashira, worshipped by gods and gandharvas."}},{"n":14,"text":"अस्त्रं ब्रह्मशिरो नाम देवगन्धर्वपूजितम् ।\nतदद्य मयि दाशार्ह यथा पितरि मे तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now that weapon is in me, descendant of Dasharha, as it was in my father."}},{"n":15,"text":"अस्मत्तस्तदुपादाय दिव्यमस्त्रं यदूत्तम ।\nममाप्यस्त्रं प्रयच्छ त्वं चक्रं रिपुहरं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking that divine weapon from me, best of the Yadus, give me too your discus, the weapon that destroys foes in battle.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"स राजन्प्रीयमाणेन मयाप्युक्तः कृताञ्जलिः ।\nयाचमानः प्रयत्नेन मत्तोऽस्त्रं भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, king, he asked me with joined hands, pleaded earnestly, O best of the Bharatas, and I, being pleased, replied to him."}},{"n":17,"text":"देवदानवगन्धर्वमनुष्यपतगोरगाः ।\nन समा मम वीर्यस्य शतांशेनापि पिण्डिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Gods, danavas, gandharvas, men, birds and serpents, all gathered together, are not equal to a hundredth part of my strength."}},{"n":18,"text":"इदं धनुरियं शक्तिरिदं चक्रमियं गदा ।\nयद्यदिच्छसि चेदस्त्रं मत्तस्तत्तद्ददानि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here is this bow, this spear, this discus, this mace; whichever weapon you wish from me, I will give it to you."}},{"n":19,"text":"यच्छक्नोषि समुद्यन्तुं प्रयोक्तुमपि वा रणे ।\nतद्गृहाण विनास्त्रेण यन्मे दातुमभीप्ससि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take whatever you can lift, or even wield in battle, without giving me the weapon you wish to give me.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"स सुनाभं सहस्रारं वज्रनाभमयस्मयम् ।\nवव्रे चक्रं महाबाहो स्पर्धमानो मया सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, mighty-armed one, rivaling me, he chose the iron discus with its fine hub, thousand spokes and thunderbolt-hard nave."}},{"n":21,"text":"गृहाण चक्रमित्युक्तो मया तु तदनन्तरम् ।\nजग्राहोपेत्य सहसा चक्रं सव्येन पाणिना ।\nन चैतदशकत्स्थानात्संचालयितुमच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I said \"Take the discus,\" he came up and suddenly seized the discus with his left hand, but could not move it from its place, unshaken one."}},{"n":22,"text":"अथ तद्दक्षिणेनापि ग्रहीतुमुपचक्रमे ।\nसर्वयत्नेन तेनापि गृह्णन्नेतदकल्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he tried to grasp it with his right hand too, and though he took hold of it with all his effort, he could not budge it."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः सर्वबलेनापि यच्चैतन्न शशाक सः ।\nउद्धर्तुं वा चालयितुं द्रौणिः परमदुर्मनाः ।\nकृत्वा यत्नं परं श्रान्तः स न्यवर्तत भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, though he used all his strength, Drona's son, very troubled, could not lift or move it; having made a great effort, he gave up exhausted, O Bharata."}},{"n":24,"text":"निवृत्तमथ तं तस्मादभिप्रायाद्विचेतसम् ।\nअहमामन्त्र्य सुस्निग्धमश्वत्थामानमब्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had turned back from that desire, bewildered, I called him over and said to Ashvatthaman, who was very dear to me:"}},{"n":25,"text":"यः स देवमनुष्येषु प्रमाणं परमं गतः ।\nगाण्डीवधन्वा श्वेताश्वः कपिप्रवरकेतनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He who has become the highest measure among gods and men, the wielder of the Gandiva, with white horses and a great ape on his banner,"}},{"n":26,"text":"यः साक्षाद्देवदेवेशं शितिकण्ठमुमापतिम् ।\nद्वंद्वयुद्धे पराजिष्णुस्तोषयामास शंकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"who, wanting victory in single combat, pleased the very god of gods, the blue-throated lord of Uma, Shankara himself,"}},{"n":27,"text":"यस्मात्प्रियतरो नास्ति ममान्यः पुरुषो भुवि ।\nनादेयं यस्य मे किंचिदपि दाराः सुतास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"than whom no other man on earth is dearer to me, and to whom there is nothing I would not give, neither wife nor sons,"}},{"n":28,"text":"तेनापि सुहृदा ब्रह्मन्पार्थेनाक्लिष्टकर्मणा ।\nनोक्तपूर्वमिदं वाक्यं यत्त्वं मामभिभाषसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"even he, my friend Partha of untiring deeds, never said to me what you are saying to me now, brahmin."}},{"n":29,"text":"ब्रह्मचर्यं महद्घोरं चीर्त्वा द्वादशवार्षिकम् ।\nहिमवत्पार्श्वमभ्येत्य यो मया तपसार्चितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After performing a great and terrible twelve years of celibacy, I went to the side of the Himalaya and worshipped him with austerity."}},{"n":30,"text":"समानव्रतचारिण्यां रुक्मिण्यां योऽन्वजायत ।\nसनत्कुमारस्तेजस्वी प्रद्युम्नो नाम मे सुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And my son Pradyumna, radiant like Sanatkumara, who was born to Rukmini, who kept the same vow with me,"}},{"n":31,"text":"तेनाप्येतन्महद्दिव्यं चक्रमप्रतिमं मम ।\nन प्रार्थितमभून्मूढ यदिदं प्रार्थितं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"even he never asked, fool, for this great, divine, matchless discus of mine, as you have asked."}},{"n":32,"text":"रामेणातिबलेनैतन्नोक्तपूर्वं कदाचन ।\nन गदेन न साम्बेन यदिदं प्रार्थितं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty Rama never said this, nor Gada, nor Samba, as you have asked."}},{"n":33,"text":"द्वारकावासिभिश्चान्यैर्वृष्ण्यन्धकमहारथैः ।\nनोक्तपूर्वमिदं जातु यदिदं प्रार्थितं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor have the other great charioteers of the Vrishnis and Andhakas, dwelling at Dvaraka, ever said what you have asked."}},{"n":34,"text":"भारताचार्यपुत्रः सन्मानितः सर्वयादवैः ।\nचक्रेण रथिनां श्रेष्ठ किं नु तात युयुत्ससे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the son of the teacher of the Bharatas and honored by all the Yadavas; best of charioteers, dear one, what do you mean to fight with this discus?\""}},{"n":35,"text":"एवमुक्तो मया द्रौणिर्मामिदं प्रत्युवाच ह ।\nप्रयुज्य भवते पूजां योत्स्ये कृष्ण त्वयेत्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed by me, Drona's son replied: \"I will worship you with the weapon and fight you, Krishna."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततस्ते प्रार्थितं चक्रं देवदानवपूजितम् ।\nअजेयः स्यामिति विभो सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I asked for your discus, worshipped by gods and danavas, so that I might be unconquerable; this I tell you truly, lord."}},{"n":37,"text":"त्वत्तोऽहं दुर्लभं काममनवाप्यैव केशव ।\nप्रतियास्यामि गोविन्द शिवेनाभिवदस्व माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without attaining from you the wish that is hard to get, Keshava, I will go back; speak to me kindly, Govinda."}},{"n":38,"text":"एतत्सुनाभं वृष्णीनामृषभेण त्वया धृतम् ।\nचक्रमप्रतिचक्रेण भुवि नान्योऽभिपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"This fine-hubbed discus is carried by you, bull of the Vrishnis, and there is no one on earth to match it.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"एतावदुक्त्वा द्रौणिर्मां युग्यमश्वान्धनानि च ।\nआदायोपययौ बालो रत्नानि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the young Drona's son took chariot horses, wealth and many kinds of jewels, and went away."}},{"n":40,"text":"स संरम्भी दुरात्मा च चपलः क्रूर एव च ।\nवेद चास्त्रं ब्रह्मशिरस्तस्माद्रक्ष्यो वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is hot-headed, evil-minded, fickle and cruel, and he knows the Brahmashira weapon; therefore Vrikodara must be protected."}}]}]}